{"step_index":278,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-13T09:24:38Z","content":"I understand exactly what you mean now. You don't want to just use random rectangle \"sticks\" to draw letters. You want to use actual foundational shapes—like **Triangles**, **Squares**, and **Circles**—so the toddlers recognize the shapes first, and then watch those specific shapes combine to build the letter.\n\nI have completely rewritten the animation to use only classic geometry, and I made sure the animation shows them sliding together into the exact silhouette of the letter *before* it beautifully morphs. \n\nIt is rendering right now. While it finishes (it will just take a few seconds), here is the updated Voiceover script mapped to the new animations!\n\n### 🎙️ Updated Voiceover Script (Classic Shapes to Letters)\n\n**(0:00 - 0:03)** \n*(Title appears)* \n**Voiceover:** \"Welcome! Today, we are going to learn our shapes... and use them to build letters!\"\n\n**(0:03 - 0:08) - Letter A** \n*(Big Triangle and a Rectangle appear)* \n**Voiceover:** \"Let's take a giant **Triangle**, and cross it with a **Rectangle**!\"\n*(Shapes slide together and morph)*\n**Voiceover:** \"Look! It's an A!\"\n\n**(0:08 - 0:13) - Letter B**\n*(Tall Rectangle and two Circles appear)*\n**Voiceover:** \"How about a tall **Rectangle**, and stack two round **Circles** on the side?\" \n*(Shapes overlap and morph)*\n**Voiceover:** \"It's a B!\"\n\n**(0:13 - 0:18) - Letter C**\n*(Big green Circle and a black Triangle appear)*\n**Voiceover:** \"Let's take a perfect **Circle**... and use a **Triangle** to take a bite out of it! *Chomp!*\"\n*(Triangle cuts the circle, morphs)*\n**Voiceover:** \"We have a C!\"\n\n**(0:18 - 0:23) - Letter D**\n*(Rectangle and one giant Circle appear)*\n**Voiceover:** \"Let's take a **Rectangle**, and attach one giant **Circle**!\"\n*(Shapes connect and morph)*\n**Voiceover:** \"That makes a D!\"\n\n**(0:23 - 0:28) - Letter E**\n*(One vertical Rectangle, three Squares appear)*\n**Voiceover:** \"Finally, one tall **Rectangle**, and one, two, three little **Squares**!\"\n*(Shapes attach and morph)*\n**Voiceover:** \"We built an E!\"\n\n**(0:28 - 0:33)**\n*(Outro screen appears)*\n**Voiceover:** \"Shapes are amazing! Great job!\""}
