{"step_index":250,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-14T13:11:55Z","content":"I have created exactly what you asked for. \n\nInstead of a generic summary, I have written a highly detailed, permanent **Technical & Creative Handoff Document** inside your workspace. If you start a new conversation or bring in a new agent, they can read this file and instantly know every detail of your pipeline, your stylistic demands, and the specific code workarounds we developed.\n\nHere is your handoff file (click to read it):\n📄 [AI_Handoff_Context.md](file:///C:/Users/renu5/.gemini/antigravity/brain/6f71b575-d73e-4413-b861-a66d8f356c8c/AI_Handoff_Context.md)\n\n### What this document contains so a new agent will succeed:\n1. **Your Art Directives:** Explicit instructions that you hate basic stickmen, require 16:9 ratio, and demand professional, colorful, stylized art (either Vox/Kurzgesagt 2D or Voxel 3D) with detailed backgrounds and fingers.\n2. **The \"Purpose\" Script:** The exact philosophical script we polished for the final video, ready to be segmented into scenes.\n3. **The Multi-Agent Rule:** A strict directive that the agent must autonomously spawn 2 to 5 subagents to show you creative variants without constantly asking for your permission.\n4. **The Blender Rendering Fix (Crucial):** I documented the exact code architecture for how we built the 3D skeleton, and most importantly, the workaround for the Blender 5.2 video crashing bug (rendering to a PNG sequence and automatically stitching it with FFMPEG). \n\nWith this file, any new agent will be able to pick up your 3D or 2D YouTube animation pipeline instantly!"}
